    {
      "id": "98f84a51135e24048f79217fd08652745257a797",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1901523816,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Why do we change all the lua_Number/lua_Integer for release-4.2 when we don't build with Lua 5.3 or Lua 5.4?\n\nI think also the changes done in `File_seek()` is wrong because an offset is not a float, but it doesn't matter when not building with Lua 5.3 or Lua 5.4.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/905aafc6b50e246885f5ea9273a9dc4f22e2658b71f9a1b551b797082bec3f80?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/stigbjorlykke"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-05-11T10:24:42.947Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-05-11T10:24:42.947Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 301105583,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 15584,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6d7f5e221c09438a04ba1cb61c62eea23cd1e407",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1901536148,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Why do we change all the lua_Number/lua_Integer for release-4.2 when we don't build with Lua 5.3 or Lua 5.4?\n\nI don't know, it doesn't make sense.\n\nYes, the `File_seek()` one is also wrong. I think it does make a difference when building with 32-bit Lua and large file support, because it will cast to a 32-bit `ptrdiff_t`. We don't currently have 32-bit CI (#19789) though our tests don't test for that case.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-05-11T11:11:56.655Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-05-11T11:52:47.232Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 301105583,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 15584,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1901541675,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Should we revert all changes to release-4.2 and concentrate on making the 4.4 release support Lua 5.3 and Lua 5.4?",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/905aafc6b50e246885f5ea9273a9dc4f22e2658b71f9a1b551b797082bec3f80?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/stigbjorlykke"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-05-11T11:52:47.162Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-05-11T11:52:47.162Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 301105583,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 15584,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1901545047,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Possibly so. We released 4.2.4 with the changes, but it should have done much on Lua 5.1 and 5.2 other than (sometimes incorrect on 32 bit systems) bounds checking and casts.\n\nDo we want to support 32 bit Lua 5.3 and 5.4 (not the same as 32 bit platforms)? Note that treating 32 bit unsigned integers as Lua Integers freely requires Lua with 64 bit Integers, or else it will be cast to negative numbers with certain uses.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-05-11T12:18:54.249Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-05-11T12:18:54.249Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 301105583,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 15584,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1901553723,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Hi,\nAt the start it made sense to backport lua changes as it keep options open\nto move to later lua versions if platforms dropped support for older lua\nversions.\n\nNow it seems less straightforward.\n\nskrev:",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-05-11T13:10:14.630Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-05-11T13:10:14.630Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 301105583,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 15584,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1901556051,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Ah, the idea is 4.2.x will be supported until 2025, and some platforms may drop Lua 5.2 by then? I think we would just recommend 4.4 to people in that situation.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-05-11T13:17:52.134Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-05-11T13:17:52.134Z",
